  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. copper exports were $12.61B in 2025 (+3.2%) and $10.70B in January–August 2026 (+30.3%). Copper scrap (7404, $6.01B) is half of the total and now goes mainly to Japan, Korea, Thailand, India and the EU, not China.",
    "China charges 35% on U.S. copper scrap and cathode unless the importer holds an exclusion. The exclusions end December 31, 2026, and the suspension of 24 points of China's extra duty ends January 10, 2027.",
    "Canada has charged a 50% surtax on U.S. refined copper wire (7408.11, 7408.19) since September 8, 2026, even on wire that qualifies for CUSMA. Canadian manufacturers that use the wire can claim the surtax back.",
    "Mexico, the largest buyer ($3.96B, mostly cathode and wire rod), charges 0% on qualifying copper under USMCA. Its January 2026 tariff increases left Chapter 74 alone."
  ],
